# If you prefer the allow list template instead of the deny list, see community template:
# https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/community/Golang/Go.AllowList.gitignore
#
# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test
.playwright-mcp

# Code coverage profiles and other test artifacts
*.out
coverage.*
*.coverprofile
profile.cov

# Dependency directories (remove the comment below to include it)
# vendor/

# Go workspace file
go.work
go.work.sum

# env file
.env

# Editor/IDE
# .idea/
# .vscode/


# Scratch notes (never commit)
/scratch/

# reactorcide run-local writes this summary at the repo root
/reactorcide-workflow-summary.json

# Security audit working notes / triage (never commit)
/sec-explore/

# --- Build artifacts and fetched dependencies, every language ---
#
# NOTE: a comment must be on its OWN line. Git only treats a line as a comment
# when it STARTS with '#', so `target/   # Rust` is a pattern that literally
# contains spaces and the word Rust, and it matches nothing. Ten patterns in
# this block were written that way and were silently dead, which is how
# crates/linkkeys/loadtest/target/ (1.2 GiB, 9871 files) reached a commit.
# Verify any change here with `git check-ignore -v <path>`, not by eye.

# Rust. Unanchored, so it covers every crate with its own target dir, not just
# the workspace root: crates/linkkeys/loadtest/ and sdks/local-rp/rust/ are
# both outside the root workspace and build into their own.
target/

# OCaml (dune) and Elixir (mix)
_build/
# OCaml local switch
_opam/

# Node and TypeScript fetched dependencies
node_modules/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/

# Dart
.dart_tool/

# Zig
zig-out/
zig-cache/
.zig-cache/

# Gradle (Java/Kotlin)
.gradle/

# Erlang/Elixir
*.beam

# C
*.o
*.a
